# Backend JavaScript

Apply when editing backend `.js` / `.mjs` / `.cjs` files. Prefer existing patterns in `backend/` over inventing new structure.

## Structure

```text
backend/src/modules/<feature>/
  <feature>.module.js
  <feature>.controller.js
  <feature>.service.js
  <feature>.repository.js
  dto/
  types/
```

## Layering

- Controllers/routes: transport, validation, auth guards, response mapping only.
- Services: business logic and workflows.
- Repositories: persistence only.
- Do not put business logic or direct DB access in controllers.

## Conventions

- Use ES modules unless the file already uses CommonJS; match neighbors.
- Prefer `async`/`await` over raw promise chains.
- Reuse existing guards, middleware, exceptions, and utilities.
- Keep modules cohesive; avoid circular dependencies.
- Do not change DB schema without a migration when migrations are used.
- Do not invent public API or schema changes without an explicit request.

## Example

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — DB + business logic in controller
async function createUser(req, res) {
  const user = await db.users.insert(req.body);
  res.json(user);
}

// ✅ GOOD — controller delegates to service
async function createUser(req, res) {
  const user = await userService.create(req.body);
  res.status(201).json(user);
}
```
